## Systems Architecture (by Planes)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  %% =========================
  %% Systems Architecture View
  %% Grouped into Planes
  %% =========================

  %% ---- Control Plane ----
  subgraph CP[Control Plane (API + Orchestration)]
    CP1[NestJS API Gateway\n(Auth/JWT, REST)]
    CP2[Thread & Agent Services\n(thread state, agent spec, policy)]
    CP3[Model Router\n(task class + risk + latency)\n→ model + budget]
    CP4[Responses API Client\n(text + tools + JSON + streaming)]
    CP5[Tool Policy Engine\n(allowlist, scopes, escalation)]
  end

  %% ---- Data Plane ----
  subgraph DP[Data Plane (State + Retrieval)]
    DP1[MongoDB\nThreads, Users, Receipts]
    DP2[Vector Index (Mongo)\nEmbeddings: text-embedding-3-small]
    DP3[Artifacts Store\n(agent specs, suggestion blocks)]
  end

  %% ---- Event Plane ----
  subgraph EP[Event Plane (Streaming + Jobs + Observability)]
    EP1[WebSocket / Socket.IO\nToken + Tool Lifecycle Events]
    EP2[Redis + BullMQ\nIndexing, async tool jobs]
    EP3[Metrics/Tracing\nTTFT, tool latency, schema pass rate]
  end

  %% ---- Session Plane ----
  subgraph SP[Session Plane (Realtime Sessions)]
    SP1[LiveKit Session Runtime\nVoice worker]
    SP2[OpenAI RealtimeModel\nInterruptible voice]
    SP3[Avatar Session (Hedra)\nOptional visual presence]
    SP4[MCP Tools (Firecrawl)\nWeb search/scrape via MCP server]
  end

  %% ---- UI ----
  UI[Client UI\n(Chat + Agent State)]

  %% ======= Flows =======
  UI -->|messages| CP1
  CP1 --> CP2
  CP2 -->|load thread state| DP1
  CP2 --> CP3 --> CP4

  %% Tool execution gating
  CP4 -->|tool call proposals| CP5
  CP5 -->|exec approved tools| EP2
  EP2 -->|tool results| CP4

  %% Retrieval
  CP2 -->|retrieve| DP2 -->|scoped snippets| CP4

  %% Artifacts / receipts
  CP4 -->|write receipts + artifacts| DP1
  CP4 -->|write structured blocks| DP3

  %% Streaming back to UI
  CP4 -->|stream tokens/JSON| EP1 --> UI
  EP2 -->|tool lifecycle| EP1

  %% Realtime voice sessions
  UI -.->|voice start| SP1
  SP1 --> SP2 --> CP4
  SP1 -.-> SP3
  SP1 -->|web tools| SP4
  SP1 -->|events| EP1

  %% Observability
  CP4 --> EP3
  EP2 --> EP3
  EP1 --> EP3
